这是那种你还不太清楚自己是谁的阶段。

00:08:24.639 --> 00:08:29.160
The cement has not dried on you or your career or where you're standing in life at all.
你的人生、你的事业或你所处的地位，一切都还没定型。

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.139
and you're like, wait, where the fuck am I?
你会想，等等，我到底在哪儿？

00:08:31.139 --> 00:08:34.820
And I'm impressed with this in this rewatch so far.
到目前为止，重温这一集让我印象深刻。

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:38.080
Here we are, middle of season three, further than middle.
我们现在处于第三季的中段，甚至比中段还要靠后。

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.820
And there's a lot of good stuff about career, just what you just said.
关于事业有很多好的内容，就像你刚才说的那样。

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:49.259
There's a lot, it's this romantic comedy, that's the category it was put in, that's the shelf it would be on in the bookstore.
有很多，这是一部浪漫喜剧，这是它被归类的类别，也是书店里它会被放在的架子上。

00:08:49.259 --> 00:08:55.460
But like, we do a lot about finding yourself in other ways in your late 20s, early 30s.
但是，我们在20多岁末、30多岁初，也做了很多关于寻找自我的内容。

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:59.899
And I'd forgotten how many of those are good, how many episodes of that or hold their weight?
我忘了有多少集是好的，有多少集是经得起时间考验的？

00:08:59.899 --> 00:09:14.019
This might be waiting into kind of territory that we would dance around delicately, but I think part of wanting a good career is you want to be attractive to a mate.
这可能涉及到我们通常会小心翼翼避开的领域，但我认为想要一份好事业的部分原因，是你想要吸引伴侣。

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:14.860
Yeah.
是的。

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:26.620
And you want to be able to provide for your wife and your future, your imaginary wife and your imaginary children, yeah, there's a lot that goes and they're not, what I'm saying is they're inextricably linked.
你想要有能力供养你的妻子和未来，你想象中的妻子和想象中的孩子，是的，有很多因素，它们是密不可分的。

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.460
Yeah.
是的。

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:38.957
search for romance, the search for love and connection and partnership in your 20s and 30s, and your ambition and your wanting to make a name for yourself and achieve in the industry you've chosen.
在20多岁和30多岁时对浪漫的追求，对爱、联系和伴侣关系的追求，以及你的野心，你想要出人头地，在你选择的行业中取得成就。

00:09:38.957 --> 00:09:43.860
Those are really woven together in ways that I don't think people talk about enough.
这些真的交织在一起，我觉得人们谈论得还不够多。

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.702
Yeah, I mean, it's part of this.
是的，我的意思是，这是其中的一部分。

00:09:45.702 --> 00:09:56.179
We always talk about how there's this kind of second adolescence at the end of your 20s into your 30s, and it's maybe the more important one, and you're not really an adult yet then.
我们总是谈论在20多岁末到30多岁初有一种“第二次青春期”，这可能是更重要的一次，那时你还不是真正的成年人。

00:09:56.179 --> 00:09:59.860
And I think this is one of those moments of like, what kind of grown up am I becoming?
我认为这是其中一个时刻，就像，我正在成为什么样的成年人？

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:04.539
Am I becoming the kind of grown up who can get screamed at on a Tuesday morning?
我正在成为那种可以在周二早上被大吼大叫的成年人吗？

00:10:04.539 --> 00:10:06.539
And I'm just supposed to act like that's okay.
而我只是应该表现得好像这没关系一样。

00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:14.620
And it's such a glimpse into Barney's world and who he is, it is like, I got screamed at three times today, it's just like, do I want to live a life where that's normal?
这真是对巴尼的世界和他本人的一个窥视，就像是，我今天被吼了三次，这就像是，我想要过那种生活吗？

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:19.700
The shot where they introduced Blowman and Billson, is Brian's character Billson?
介绍布洛曼和比尔森的那个镜头，布莱恩的角色是比尔森吗？

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:20.620
Is that Billson?
那是比尔森吗？

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:26.980
Okay, so Billson and Blowman, which I would say are in the Mount Rushmore of a hymnium side character.
好吧，所以是比尔森和布洛曼，我会说他们是《老爸老妈浪漫史》配角中的“总统山”级别。

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.419
Side character is absolutely.
绝对是配角。

00:10:28.419 --> 00:10:31.299
Ghost of the Lamen is an unbelievable combo.
“拉曼之鬼”是一个令人难以置信的组合。

00:10:31.299 --> 00:10:38.139
But the shot, the pan across the conference room of Barney's, the guys he works with.
但是那个镜头，扫过巴尼的会议室，他一起工作的那些人。

00:10:38.139 --> 00:10:43.539
And just the ease that with which he's just slouched in that chair looking at his phone.
他瘫在椅子上看手机的那种轻松感。

00:10:43.539 --> 00:10:45.340
He's not even noticing the screaming.
他甚至没注意到尖叫声。

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:46.899
He's like, he's texting.
他在发短信。

00:10:46.899 --> 00:10:51.500
And he only pricks up when a guy starts to try to urinate on the conference table.
只有当有人开始试图在会议桌上小便时，他才抬起头。

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.980
That's the only thing that suddenly that rates a little bit of attention.
那是唯一能引起他一点点注意的事情。

00:10:54.980 --> 00:11:04.759
And I wrote you this little ditty to sing to you in New York City.
我给你写了这首小曲子，要在纽约市唱给你听。

00:11:04.759 --> 00:11:18.200
We'll be right back, back to the show.
我们马上回来，回到节目中。

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:23.399
That little scene, every now and again in life, as writers or artists, whatever, you get to steal something.
那个小场景，作为作家或艺术家，生活中偶尔会有机会去“偷”点东西。

00:11:23.399 --> 00:11:24.399
You never knew what to do.
你永远不知道该做什么。

00:11:24.399 --> 00:11:26.600
You know, you have some idea and you're like, I don't know what that is.
你知道，你有一些想法，你会想，我不知道那是什么。

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.120
I don't know what I'll ever do with that.
我不知道我以后会用它做什么。

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:32.200
I just, when I was in a job, I was ready to be out of one time.
我只是，当我在一份工作时，我曾想过要离开。

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:35.720
I imagined a short film, and this was the short film.
我构思了一部短片，这就是那部短片。

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:39.639
The short film was, a guy comes in, and this is his plan.
短片的内容是，一个人走进来，这就是他的计划。

00:11:39.639 --> 00:11:50.279
He's gonna get him on the conference room table, give him a big speech, unzip, and just fucking fire hose all over that conference room table, and then he can't, he has stage, right?
他要让他们在会议桌上，发表一番长篇大论，拉开拉链，然后对着会议桌喷射，然后他就有舞台了，对吧？

00:11:50.279 --> 00:11:53.559
And it was just like a random short film idea, like I jotted it down in a notebook.
这只是一个随机的短片点子，我把它记在笔记本上。

00:11:53.559 --> 00:11:56.480
I'm like, I'm not going to make this short film.
我想，我不会拍这部短片。

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:03.480
The world doesn't need a short film, but what better plot to us for Blowman?
世界不需要这部短片，但对于布洛曼来说，还有什么比这更好的情节呢？

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:10.840
Every now and again, you find a way, when you, this is one of the joys of a long-running TV show, you're like, we could do that, we could just do that little vignette.
偶尔，你会找到一种方法，这是长篇电视剧的乐趣之一，你会想，我们可以那样做，我们可以只做那个小片段。

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:14.360
And Taryn is so funny in that scene, it's a really funny scene.
塔伦在那个场景里太搞笑了，那是一个非常有趣的场景。

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:20.759
Well, it's almost like the best, the best thievery is from yourself as a writer, you know?
嗯，这几乎就像是，最好的“偷窃”是作为作家从你自己那里偷，你知道吗？

00:12:20.759 --> 00:12:23.759
It feels the best.
感觉最棒。

00:12:23.759 --> 00:12:48.480
You know, what else is really interesting about this watching it 20 years on, I feel like when we did this episode, you know, 2008, there was still this idea, especially like, you know, doing a mail room at an agency or working with, say, Scott Rudin, where you knew that you were going to be kind of abused in a, there were those famous yellers, Scott Rudin was well-known.
你知道，20年后重温这一集，还有什么非常有趣的地方，我觉得我们在2008年做这一集时，仍然有这种想法，特别是在代理公司的收发室工作，或者和斯科特·鲁丁这样的人一起工作，你知道你会受到某种虐待，那些著名的咆哮者，斯科特·鲁丁很有名。

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:54.600
Then a kind of like byproduct of me too was it was like, it wasn't just about sexual, It was like emotional abuse.
后来，“Me Too”运动的一个副产品是，它不仅仅是关于性，而是关于情感虐待。

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:55.960
And people don't abuse people.
人们不应该虐待他人。

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:56.799
Don't abuse people.
不要虐待他人。

00:12:56.799 --> 00:12:58.240
Like that is not acceptable.
那是不可以接受的。

00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:02.919
And I don't think that like the younger generations, like they won't stand for that.
我不认为年轻一代会容忍这一点。

00:13:02.919 --> 00:13:07.960
Like they will not be yelled at in that way, which I think is a good thing.
他们不会那样被吼叫，我认为这是一件好事。

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:12.480
Like I've never believed in like, you know, drill sergeant kind of bosses.
我从来不相信那种“魔鬼教官”式的老板。

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:19.600
I just think it's a, but there's something about it used to be this bit, like a bit of a rite of passage.
我只是觉得，但这曾经是一种“成人礼”。

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:27.480
Like if you could withstand, for instance, My friend of mine was Scott Rudin's assistant for about eight or nine months, which was long.
比如如果你能承受，例如，我的一个朋友给斯科特·鲁丁当了八九个月的助理，这已经很长了。

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:29.200
That was a long tenure.
那是一段很长的任期。

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.480
That's really long.
那真的很长。

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:32.240
That is a veteran to last eight months.
那是一个能坚持八个月的资深员工。

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:37.200
And afterwards, if you had that on your resume, you could kind of call your shot for your next job.
之后，如果你的简历上有这段经历，你下一份工作几乎可以随心所欲地挑选。

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:38.039
Like, wow.
就像，哇。

00:13:38.039 --> 00:13:44.240
Yeah, like everyone knew, like if you had weathered that, you were made of some strong stuff.
是啊，大家都知道，如果你能熬过那段日子，说明你是个狠角色。

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:46.600
You were a marathon runner, you had climbed Everest.
你就像跑完了马拉松，爬上了珠穆朗玛峰。

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:47.160
Yeah.
没错。

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:47.720
Yeah.
是啊。

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:57.495
It's, I mean, of course, there are still places this is the culture, plenty of them, and probably more, and now it is, I would say, in our current climate of America.
我的意思是，当然，现在依然有很多地方存在这种文化，甚至可能更多，尤其是在我们当今的美国社会环境下。

00:13:57.495 --> 00:14:04.503
But it is certainly a question you want to ask yourself, do you want to, am I signing up for a life where this is okay?
但这确实是一个你需要问自己的问题：你是否愿意，我是否在签署一份生活契约，接受这种现状？

00:14:04.503 --> 00:14:10.098
And this like, karmic idea of like, you should totally yell at the person, you have power over.
还有这种所谓的“业力”观念，即你应该对那些你拥有权力的人大吼大叫。

00:14:10.098 --> 00:14:14.986
And Barney's whole solution is, go yell at this guy bringing you food at the diner.
而巴尼的全部解决方案就是，去对那个给你送餐的餐馆服务员大吼大叫。

00:14:14.986 --> 00:14:20.640
It just is like, well, you've got to get it Now it's somewhere, it really is, it's karma, right?
这就像是，好吧，你得找个地方发泄，这真的是所谓的“业力”，对吧？

00:14:20.639 --> 00:14:22.360
We're studying the idea of karma.
我们正在研究业力的概念。

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:25.440
And it's, do you perpetuate the cycle of abuse?
问题是，你是否在延续这种虐待的循环？

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:32.320
I think a lot of people have this in there, like their parents were a certain way, they grew up a certain way, how did they then treat their kids?
我觉得很多人都有这种困扰，比如他们的父母就是那样，他们是在那种环境下长大的，那他们后来又是怎么对待自己的孩子的呢？

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:34.039
It's just this idea of, do you end it?
这其实就是个想法：你是选择终结它？

00:14:34.039 --> 00:14:35.519
Or do you perpetuate it?
还是选择延续它？

00:14:35.519 --> 00:14:42.159
And Barney is pro-perpetuating the yowl, he's like, yeah, just yell at someone that's powerful than you, that should clear it up.
而巴尼是支持延续这种咆哮的，他觉得，没错，就去对那些比你权力小的人大吼大叫，这应该能解决问题。

00:14:42.159 --> 00:14:51.399
Well, it's also, it goes in a little bit of the book of like look at what Barney doesn't do the opposite to live a good, you know, virtuous life.
嗯，这也有一点像书里说的，看看巴尼为了过上一种好的、有道德的生活，他反而没有去做相反的事情。

00:14:51.399 --> 00:14:52.240
Yeah.
没错。

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:58.799
And you know, there's also so much in comedy around punching up, punching down.
而且你知道，喜剧里关于“向上拳击”和“向下拳击”的讨论也很多。

00:14:58.799 --> 00:15:08.519
And you know, the truism is like punch up, punch, punch the powerful, don't punch the less powerful, like don't punch people that have less power and privilege than you do.
众所周知的道理是：要向上拳击，去攻击那些有权势的人，不要向下拳击，不要去攻击那些权力或特权比你少的人。

00:15:08.519 --> 00:15:09.360
So.
所以。

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:10.200
Amen.
说得好。

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.039
Yeah.
没错。

00:15:11.039 --> 00:15:16.538
But you know, it was, it's great to watch Barney be like we say confidently wrong.
但你知道，看着巴尼那种我们所说的“自信地犯错”真的很有趣。

00:15:16.538 --> 00:15:28.273
He's just so confidently wrong in the midst of like Marshall is still trying to crack the code and speak the language of corporate culture because he's not to the man or born.
他错得那么自信，而马修还在努力破解密码，试图学习企业文化的语言，因为他并不是那种天生的职场人。

00:15:28.273 --> 00:15:30.619
Like this is not his native tongue.
这并不是他的母语。

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:37.671
But yeah, I found myself really liking the stakes of Marshall saying it's a very little line in the episode.
但我确实发现自己真的很喜欢马修所面临的困境，虽然在剧集中这只是一句很短的台词。

00:15:37.671 --> 00:15:46.419
He just says, Lily supported me through law school and now it's my turn to pay her back and just that is a very adult pressure, right?
他只是说，莉莉在我读法学院时支持我，现在轮到我回报她了，这是一种非常成人的压力，对吧？

00:15:46.419 --> 00:15:49.659
That's Marshall going, I need to do this for her.
那是马修在想，我需要为她做这件事。

00:15:49.659 --> 00:15:52.820
I need to suffer through this to pay for our life.
我需要忍受这一切来维持我们的生活。

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:55.220
And that's a very real thing, right?
这非常真实，对吧？

00:15:55.220 --> 00:16:02.700
And it just, I'm gonna give up, I'm gonna now be miserable for a bunch of years because I need to pay this mortgage and Lily supported me.
就像是，我要放弃自我，我要在接下来的几年里过得痛苦不堪，因为我需要支付房贷，而且莉莉曾经支持过我。

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:07.929
And I love that little scene between them at the end where Lily goes like, no, don't do that.
我很喜欢最后他们之间那个小场景，莉莉说，不，别那样做。

00:16:07.929 --> 00:16:10.409
We're gonna figure this out somehow.
我们会想办法解决的。

00:16:10.409 --> 00:16:12.570
I can't have you be miserable like this.
我不能让你过得这么痛苦。

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:16.049
And it's just, it's very sweet and supportive, that little scene between the two of them.
那段戏非常甜蜜且充满支持，他们俩之间的那个小场景。

00:16:16.049 --> 00:16:21.610
And it doesn't solve the problem, Marshall, they, but she says we can, we're gonna figure this out.
虽然这并没有解决马修的问题，但她说我们可以，我们会想办法解决的。

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:31.210
And I was, I felt a lot of relief watching that for Marshall, because I think as someone's as men and certainly men of a certain age growing up, you have this feeling like I, but I must provide.
看着马修的这一幕，我感到如释重负，因为我觉得作为男人，尤其是成长过程中特定年龄段的男人，你会有一种感觉：我必须提供经济支持。

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.129
This is what men do.
这就是男人该做的。

00:16:32.129 --> 00:16:34.169
We shall start to provide.
我们必须开始提供保障。

00:16:34.169 --> 00:16:38.809
And I just liked Lilly saying, no, I like happy, I like happy Marshall.
我真的很喜欢莉莉说“不，我喜欢快乐，我喜欢快乐的马修”。

00:16:38.809 --> 00:16:39.809
I want that guy.
我想要那个他。

00:16:39.809 --> 00:16:43.210
That was sweet, they're a good couple.
那很甜蜜，他们是一对好夫妻。

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:49.649
It's not worth the trade-off, you know, like what you're getting and then who you become as a result.
这不值得付出这种代价，你知道，你得到了什么，以及你最终变成了什么样的人。

00:16:49.649 --> 00:16:51.570
And then you have no energy left for your relationship.
然后你对你的关系就没有任何精力了。

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.570
Like the person you fell in love with is not- And she's not getting any.
就像你爱上的那个人不再是……而且她也得不到任何东西。

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:54.570
She's not getting any.
她得不到任何东西。

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:58.570
She's totally, she's what she needs to have emotional and wants to- Yeah.
她完全……她需要情感上的支持，想要……没错。

00:16:58.570 --> 00:17:00.129
That's the party.
这就是重点。

00:17:00.129 --> 00:17:01.129
Yeah.
没错。

00:17:01.129 --> 00:17:07.650
I really thought it was so funny and clever and such a good use of the gang.
我真的觉得这非常有趣、聪明，而且对这群伙伴的运用非常好。

00:17:07.650 --> 00:17:12.369
Well, first of all, Bob's thing of Arthur, that's his name in the episode, right?
首先，鲍勃饰演的亚瑟，那是他在剧中的名字，对吧？

00:17:12.369 --> 00:17:18.609
Arthur's thing of like coming in and being incredibly kind to the person in the office next door.
亚瑟那种走进办公室，对隔壁同事表现得极其友善的行为。

00:17:18.609 --> 00:17:19.609
So funny.
太搞笑了。

00:17:19.609 --> 00:17:23.970
Psychopathically, just switching on a dime to script.
